These are my two biggest beefs with NetHack 3.0j3+:

1) (Pertains to all platforms) The interface for applying bags really sucks.
I hate to have to sort through my list to get to an item to take out or put
in the sack.  It should have the same interface as dropping an item, where
we get to just type in the letter of the item to be dropped/put in sack. As
it is, the interface is cumbersome enough that I never use sacks. 

2) The modal dialogs in the Macintosh version are disruptive, and obnoxious
on slow cpu's.  Let's maintain the standard NetHack interface across multiple
platforms.  Thank DevTeam that they did make the dialog boxes respond to key
presses! (But I still want to revert to the standard interface.)

